Morvinski D. Glioblastoma heterogeneity and cancer cell plasticity. Critical Reviews in Oncogenesis. 2014;19(5):327–336. doi: 10.1615/critrevoncog.2014011777. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Maia A. C., Jr., Malheiros S. M., da Rocha A. J. MR cerebral blood volume maps correlated with vascular endothelial growth factor expression and tumor grade in nonenhancing gliomas. AJNR American Journal of Neuroradiology. 2005;26(4):777–783. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Sagiuchi T., Oka H., Utsuki S., et al. Increased accumulations of N-isopropyl-p-[123I]-iodoamphetamine related to tumefactive multiple sclerosis. Annals of Nuclear Medicine. 2005;19(7):603–606. doi: 10.1007/bf02985054. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Enzinger C., Strasser-Fuchs S., Ropele S., Kapeller P., Kleinert R., Fazekas F. Tumefactive demyelinating lesions: conventional and advanced magnetic resonance imaging. Multiple Sclerosis Journal. 2005;11(2):135–139. doi: 10.1191/1352458505ms1145oa. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Bitsch A., Bruhn H., Vougioukas V. Inflammatory CNS demyelination: histopathologic correlation with in vivo quantitative proton MR spectroscopy. AJNR American Journal of Neuroradiology. 1999;20(9):1619–1627. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Cohen-Gadol A. A., DiLuna M. L., Bannykh S. I., Piepmeier J. M., Spencer D. D. Non-enhancing de novo glioblastoma: report of two cases. Neurosurgical Review. 2004;27(4):281–285. doi: 10.1007/s10143-004-0346-5. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Okamoto K., Ito J., Takahashi N., et al. MRI of high-grade astrocytic tumors: early appearance and evolution. Neuroradiology. 2002;44(5):395–402. doi: 10.1007/s00234-001-0725-3. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Landy H. J., Lee T. T., Potter P., Feun L., Markoe A. Early MRI findings in high grade glioma. Journal of Neuro-Oncology. 2000;47(1):65–72. doi: 10.1023/a:1006494604527. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. O